    {
      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "Let's denote the sides of the original triangle as \\(a = 6\\) cm, \\(b = 7\\) cm, and \\(c = 9\\) cm. The perimeter of the original triangle is:\n\n\\[\na + b + c = 6 + 7 + 9 = 22 \\text{ cm}\n\\]\n\nWe are given that the perimeter of a similar triangle is 110 cm. Let the sides of the similar triangle be \\(x\\), \\(y\\), and \\(z\\) where \\(x \\geq y \\geq z\\). The ratio of the perimeters of the similar triangles is equal to the ratio of their corresponding sides. Thus, the ratio of the sides is:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{x}{6} = \\frac{y}{7} = \\frac{z}{9} = k\n\\]\n\nwhere \\(k\\) is the ratio of the corresponding sides. Therefore, we can express \\(x\\), \\(y\\), and \\(z\\) as:\n\n\\[\nx = 6k, \\quad y = 7k, \\quad z = 9k\n\\]\n\nThe perimeter of the similar triangle is the sum of its sides:\n\n\\[\nx + y + z = 6k + 7k + 9k = 22k\n\\]\n\nWe know that this perimeter is 110 cm, so we set up the equation:\n\n\\[\n22k = 110\n\\]\n\nSolving for \\(k\\):\n\n\\[\nk = \\frac{110}{22} = 5\n\\]\n\nNow, we can find the lengths of the sides of the similar triangle:\n\n\\[\nx = 6k = 6 \\times 5 = 30 \\text{ cm}\n\\]\n\\[\ny = 7k = 7 \\times 5 = 35 \\text{ cm}\n\\]\n\\[\nz = 9k = 9 \\times 5 = 45 \\text{ cm}\n\\]\n\nThe longest side of the similar triangle is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{45}\n\\]",
